preConditionHook:
// MultiWalk's WFSafe_Xaverage, which the EasyLanguage twin calls. MEASURED
// BIT-IDENTICAL to the plain XAverage built-in AT A FIXED LENGTH:
// (wf - xa) * 1e12 printed exactly 0.0000 on all 9,646 + 8,139 bars of
// EL_XAverage_Probe.txt (@OJ 240min, chart starts 2007 and 2010), with the
// two fields character-identical on all 17,785. At a fixed emaLength there
// is nothing to choose between the two.
//
// SEED: the PRICE on the study's first calculated bar -- NOT a length-term
// simple average, which is what most textbooks and most other platforms do.
// Measured: xa equalled the bar's close on bar 1 of both runs
// (28.800000000000 and 17.450000000000) and a price-seeded twin matched on
// 9,646/9,646 and 8,139/8,139 bars. The simple-average twin was -3.4e-05 off
// at bar 100 and did not coincide until bar 334 / 382.
//
// AN EMA NEVER FORGETS ITS SEED. Unlike wfsafe_avgtruerange's rolling window
// there is no bar at which the seed drops out of a sum; it only decays at
// (1 - sf)^n. So the seed BAR is part of the specification: it is the first
// bar OnBarClose runs, ctx.CurrentBar() == 1, and it moves with both Max
// Bars Back and the chart start. Measured decay between the two chart
// starts: 5.41 apart at the later run's bar 1, 2.7e-04 at bar 100, 8.1e-11
// at bar 250, identical at print precision from bar 331 on. A mirror that
// seeds one bar off self-heals in ~330 bars and is materially wrong before.
//
// ONE STATEMENT, IN EL'S FORM: x + sf*(p - x), not sf*p + (1-sf)*x. The two
// are algebraically identical and NOT identical in floating point -- the
// probe's d3 column separated them on 67% of bars past 100 (exact multiples
// of 2^-48, up to 1.7e-13) and XAverage tracked the first form on every one.
// Do not re-associate this, for the same reason AtrProfitTarget's
// accumulator is two statements rather than one.
//
// NO WARM-UP HOLE: xa is non-zero from bar 1 (the seed) on all 17,785 probed
// bars -- no zero, no sentinel, no length-bar dead zone. Do NOT add a
// `ctx.CurrentBar() < n` guard returning 0; that is the textbook twin's
// behaviour, not EasyLanguage's.
//
// sf is computed from the raw input, not a truncated copy, because EL's
// Length slot is numeric and 2/(Length+1) is evaluated on the value passed.
//
// UNMEASURED: a walkforward LENGTH CHANGE, which is the whole reason the
// wrapper exists. No re-seed is expected (the wfsafe_adx / wfsafe_rsi shape
// -- sf recomputed per bar, state carried over; an EMA has no window to
// re-seed) but that is an expectation, so emaLength is PINNED in the grid
// until it is measured. Also unmeasured: what XAverage(...)[k] returns at a
// lag. This rule reads the CURRENT value only and needs no history.
const double emaSf = 2.0 / (emaLength + 1.0);
if (ctx.CurrentBar() == 1) {
    emaVal = close[0];
} else {
    emaVal = emaVal + emaSf * (close[0] - emaVal);
}
